<title>UK: Zeneca resumes rebound as ADRs climb.</title>
<headline>Zeneca resumes rebound as ADRs climb.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Zeneca Group Plc resumed their rebound on Tuesday after their ADRs posted solid gains in the U.S., dealers said.</p>
<p>The shares, which were hit hard on February 28 after news that the U.S. Food and Drug Administration had warned the UK pharmaceutical group about on of its manufacturing plans, were up 31p to 1867-1/2 by 1024 GMT.  </p>
<p>Dealers said the recent decline in sterling against the dollar also supported the shares.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
